  "record": {
    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "body": "The installed data answers the accuracy concern: 100 is an ordinary hit-rate value, while 255 is FF8's special always-hit value. Irvine, Rinoa, and Laguna ranged weapons use ordinary values near 100, so they do not bypass the flying rule. The real exception is Squall: every gunblade uses 255. Preserving vanilla perfect accuracy would exempt Squall's regular attacks; making the flying bonus override 255 for melee would make ranged attacks and Float more distinct, but would intentionally nerf Squall against flying enemies.",
